# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets out of it. Anything listed
# here is invisible to `docker build`, so it cannot end up in a layer even by accident.

# Local secrets. There should be none under backend/, but this is defence in depth: a stray .env
# here would otherwise be copied into the build stage and survive in the image history.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.p12
*.jks
*.key

# Build output. The image builds from source; shipping a host-built `build/` in would make the
# container's artifact depend on whatever the laptop last compiled.
build
*/build
.gradle
.kotlin
out

# VCS and tooling
.git
.github
.idea
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
.vscode

# Docs and OS noise
*.md
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
